$ node scripts/rea.mjs inspect-rpm-package --help
rea inspect-rpm-package — Inspect RPM lead, signature and header metadata without installing the package or unpacking the payload

Usage: rea inspect-rpm-package <path> [options]

Arguments:
  path  Local RPM package

Options:
  --max-file-bytes <value>            Maximum stable artifact bytes to read (default 64 MiB) (default: 67108864)
  --max-header-index-entries <value>  Maximum index entries in the signature or main header; exceeding the budget fails without treating the count as zero (default: 4096)
  --max-files <value>                 Maximum header file-inventory rows; exceeding the budget fails without a partial file list (default: 16384)
  --include-script-text               Include scriptlet source text, bounded by --max-script-bytes; never executed
  --max-script-bytes <value>          Maximum bytes of one scriptlet's stored text when include_script_text is true (default 1 MiB) (default: 1048576)
  --detail <complete|summary>         Deliver complete Evidence, or a summary with --evidence_output (default: complete)
  --evidence_output <string>          Save complete Evidence as a bundle; required for summary delivery. Never overwrites.

Custom Global Options:
  --timings  Write measured command timing to stderr.

Global Options:
  --filter-output <keys>              Filter output by key paths (e.g. foo,bar.baz,a[0,3])
  --format <toon|json|yaml|md|jsonl>  Output format
  --full-output                       Show full output envelope
  --help                              Show help
  --llms, --llms-full                 Print LLM-readable manifest
  --schema                            Show JSON Schema for command
  --token-count                       Print token count of output (instead of output)
  --token-limit <n>                   Limit output to n tokens
  --token-offset <n>                  Skip first n tokens of output
exit 0

